  "notes": "FILED ON THE MAGNITUDE TRIGGER ONLY (delta -7.2, above 5.0). NO BAND CHANGE — Developing sustained at both the published 35.9 and the assessed 28.7, so the band-crossing clause is not engaged and the band-crossing evidence test is not required. Recorded for completeness anyway. THIRD CONSECUTIVE CYCLE BELOW THE PUBLISHED VALUE: 2026-07-31 assessed 33.1; 2026-08-18 assessed 31.9 with an explicit downward watch flag; this cycle assesses 28.7 on genuinely new evidence that post-dates the 08-18 assessment. The 08-18 watch flag said \"escalate if the count dispute produces further violence\" — what followed was not violence but a UN High Commissioner adverse statement on arbitrary arrest and denial of due process, which is a stronger and more directly attributable signal. Baseline provenance was checked: the published 35.9 predates all three assessments and no cycle has yet moved it.",
